<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nikšić</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Onogošt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nikšić is the second-largest city of Montenegro, on a karst plain in the west of the country. Known in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> as Onogošt, it was an Ottoman fortress town until Montenegro captured it in 1877, a gain confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-berlin">Congress of Berlin</a> in 1878. It became an industrial centre known for its steelworks and brewery.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/niksic.jpg" alt="Nikšić" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Janusz Recław · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nik%C5%A1i%C4%87.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
